@model SoftCo.ViewModels.OrderEditViewModel

@* Which projects an order serves, and - only when it serves more than one - how its cost splits
   between them.

   Shared by the international and local order forms. Both can span projects, and a form that cannot
   express a split while its twin can is the kind of inconsistency somebody hits at the worst moment.

   The percentage box is hidden until a second project is ticked. Most orders serve one project and
   should never be asked a question with only one answer; the server sets their share to 1 whatever
   the form does, so nothing here is load-bearing. *@

<p class="sc-label">Projects</p>
<p class="sc-muted" style="font-size:.82rem">
    An order may serve more than one project &mdash; tick every project it belongs to.
</p>

<div class="sc-checks">
    @foreach (var p in Model.AllProjects)
    {
        <label class="sc-check">
            <input type="checkbox" name="ProjectIds" value="@p.Id" checked="@(Model.ProjectIds.Contains(p.Id))"
                   data-project-check="@p.Id" />
            <span>@p.Name</span>
            <span class="sc-share" data-project-share="@p.Id" hidden>
                @* Four decimal places, not two. A share is stored at six, so a third renders as
                   33.3333 - at two places three of them would come to 99.99 and the form would
                   refuse its own unchanged values. *@
                <input class="form-control sc-num" type="number" step="0.0001" min="0" max="100"
                       name="ProjectShares[@p.Id]"
                       value="@(Model.ProjectShares.TryGetValue(p.Id, out var sh) && sh is decimal v ? v.ToString("0.####") : "")" />
                <span class="sc-hint">% of cost</span>
            </span>
        </label>
    }
</div>

@* The share rule attaches its error to ProjectIds, and the forms' summaries are ModelOnly, so
   without this the save is silently refused and the form simply reappears unchanged. *@
<span asp-validation-for="ProjectIds" class="sc-error"></span>

<p class="sc-hint" data-share-hint hidden>
    This order is split across more than one project, so say how much of its cost belongs to each.
    The shares have to add up to 100%.
</p>
